  "r4": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "24. Victorious are the blessed poets-in-chief, conversant",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "with all sentiments, whose bodies in the form of fame enjoy",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "immunity from old age and death.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r5": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "25. A well-behaved son, a chaste and loving wife, a master",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "ready to bestow favours, an affectionate friend, honest ser-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "vants, the mind free from the least trouble, a lovely form,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "abiding prosperity, and a face effulgent with learning;",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "all these can be obtained by a mortal if Hari, who gratifies",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "desires and pleases the world, is propitiated.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r6": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "26. Refraining from destroying life, self-restraint as",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "regards appropriating the wealth of others, truthful speech,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "charity at the right time and according to means, not",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "talking about the young wives of others, impeding the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "stream of greed, humility towards elders, compassion for all",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "creatures—this is the way to happiness common in all the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "scriptures, that never fails in its operation ( or vitiates no",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
